      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:190:51",
      "text": [
        " تَذَاكَرُوا الشُّؤْمَ عِنْدَ أَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) فَقَالَ الشُّؤْمُ فِي ثَلَاثٍ فِي الْمَرْأَةِ وَ الدَّابَّةِ وَ الدَّارِ فَأَمَّا شُؤْمُ الْمَرْأَةِ فَكَثْرَةُ مَهْرِهَا وَ عُقْمُ رَحِمِهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "And from him, from Usman Bin Isa, from Khalid Bin Najeeh, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘They mentioned the misfortune in the presence of Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The misfortune is in three – in the woman, and the animal, and the house. So, as for the misfortune in the woman, so it is the largeness of her dower and bareness of her womb’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "51. It is narrated from the narrator of the previous Hadith from ‘Uthman ibn ‘Isa from Khalid ibn Najih who has said the following: “People mentioned misfortune before abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, and he (the Imam) said, ‘Misfortune is in three things: They are woman, a stumper and a house. Misfortune in woman is the large amount of her mahr (dower) and barren womb.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
